Sure! To update a `break` node’s label to `'loopEnd'`, you’ll want to call the `updateBreak` function like this:

```javascript
const result = updateBreak({
  node: /* your break node in string form */,
  label: "loopEnd"
});
```

Just replace `/* your break node in string form */` with the actual stringified representation of the node you want to modify. Once you run this, the function will check the current label and only change it if it isn’t already `'loopEnd'`. Let me know if you need help formatting the node or anything else!
